<!-- @before Reconnection: The Hard Part :: guide -->
### The resume carrier is only one piece

SSE defines event IDs and Last-Event-ID in its browser processing model. An Android integration still needs persisted progress, reconnect ownership, deduplication and a retention-gap outcome. WebSocket framing supplies no equivalent application replay contract. [SSE processing](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/server-sent-events.html) and [WebSocket protocol](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6455.html).

<!-- @before Answer Key :: staff -->
### Authentication refresh requires server protocol support

Answer 8 is an illustrative in-stream design, not a standard WebSocket authentication frame. If that negotiated protocol is unavailable, reconnect with fresh credentials and restore continuity through the application contract. Do not accept unvalidated refresh messages as renewed authorization.

<!-- @before Reconnection: The Hard Part :: visual -->
### The cursor and the pending edit have separate owners

```mermaid
flowchart TB
 c["Client continuation Persisted cursor C7"]
 p["Pending edit P1 Durable outbox"]
 a["Sync API Validate retained cursor"]
 b["Authoritative base Replacement snapshot"]
 c -->|"resume request"| a
 a -->|"expired cursor: full snapshot"| b
 b -->|"rebase under conflict policy"| p
```

A reset replaces the authoritative base. Pending local work remains separately owned until it is accepted, rebased, conflicted or deliberately discarded under the product contract.
